---
layout: home.njk
---
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="intro-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">{{ cv.headline }}</span>
    <h1 id="intro-heading">Words that help people <em>get things done</em></h1>
    <div class="hero__row">
      <p class="lede">I'm {{ site.name }}, a content designer in {{ site.location }} with {{ cv.years }} years' experience designing GOV.UK services at the Ministry of Justice and e-commerce journeys in retail. I work with interaction designers, user researchers and service designers from discovery to delivery, shaping structure, journeys and language.</p>
      <div>
        <ul class="swatches" aria-hidden="true">
          {%- for p in projects %}<li style="--bg: {{ p.tile.bg }}; --fg: {{ p.tile.accent }}">{{ loop.index }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
        <div class="buttons">
          <a class="button" href="#work">See the 6 projects</a>
          <a class="button button--ghost" href="#experience">My experience</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="impact" aria-labelledby="impact-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="impact__head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Selected impact</span>
      <h2 id="impact-heading">What clearer content changed</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="impact__list">
      {%- for i in cv.impact %}
      <li><strong>{{ i.value }}</strong><span>{{ i.label }}</span></li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="work" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="work__head">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Case studies</span>
        <h2 id="work-heading">Six projects, six problems</h2>
      </div>
      <p>These are self-initiated, so I can show the whole process, from the original content to every decision, artefact and check. Each one is its own site, designed to suit its subject.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="tiles">
      {%- for p in projects %}
      <li class="tile tile--{{ p.slug }}" style="--bg: {{ p.tile.bg }}; --fg: {{ p.tile.ink }}; --accent: {{ p.tile.accent }}; --tfont: {{ p.tile.font }}; --tweight: {{ p.tile.weight }}">
        <div class="tile__top"><span class="tile__num">0{{ loop.index }}</span><span class="tile__mark" aria-hidden="true">{{ p.tile.mark }}</span></div>
        <p class="tile__label">{{ p.label }}</p>
        <h3><a href="/{{ p.slug }}/">{{ p.title }}</a></h3>
        <p class="tile__stat"><strong>{{ p.tile.stat }}</strong><span>{{ p.tile.statLabel }}</span></p>
        <div class="tile__foot"><span class="tile__skills">{{ p.skills | join(" · ") }}</span><span class="tile__go" aria-hidden="true">View →</span></div>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="experience" id="experience" aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
  <div class="wrap experience__grid">
    <div class="experience__intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">Experience</span>
      <h2 id="experience-heading">{{ cv.years }} years of content design</h2>
      <p>From GOV.UK services used by the public to e-commerce journeys where every word affects conversion.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="roles">
      {%- for r in cv.roles %}
      <li class="role">
        <p class="role__dates">{{ r.dates }}</p>
        <h3>{{ r.title }}<span>{{ r.org }}, {{ r.place }}</span></h3>
        <p class="role__summary">{{ r.summary }}</p>
        <ul>
          {%- for pt in r.points %}<li>{{ pt }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
      <li class="role role--small">
        <h3>Community and practice</h3>
        <ul>
          {%- for c in cv.community %}<li>{{ c }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li class="role role--small">
        <h3>Education</h3>
        <ul class="education">
          {%- for e in cv.education %}<li><strong>{{ e.title }}</strong>{% if e.org %}, {{ e.org }}{% endif %}{% if e.detail %}<span>{{ e.detail }}</span>{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="approach" id="approach" aria-labelledby="approach-heading">
  <div class="wrap approach__grid">
    <div class="approach__intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">How I work</span>
      <h2 id="approach-heading">Every word has a reason</h2>
      <p>Good content design is mostly decisions: what to ask, what to cut, what to call things, and what comes first. I make those decisions visible, so a team can see why the words are the way they are.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="ways">
      <li>
        <h3>Start with the user need</h3>
        <p>Every project begins with what people are trying to do, and what the organisation needs from it. Both go at the top of the page, and everything is checked against them.</p>
        <a href="/council-form/">See it in the council form</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Cut what isn't needed</h3>
        <p>A question protocol or content audit shows what each question or paragraph is for. If nobody uses it, it goes. If another page does it better, it moves.</p>
        <a href="/guidance-page/">See it in the repairs page</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>One name for each thing</h3>
        <p>People lose trust when the same thing has 4 names. Terminology lists and style guides keep every channel and every writer consistent.</p>
        <a href="/touchpoints/">See it in the touchpoints project</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Decide with evidence</h3>
        <p>Research, analytics and testing settle content decisions, not opinion. I measure what can be measured, and design research like card sorts and tree tests for the rest.</p>
        <a href="/navigation/">See it in the navigation project</a>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="toolkit" id="skills" aria-labelledby="toolkit-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Skills and tools</span>
    <h2 id="toolkit-heading">Core expertise</h2>
    <ul class="expertise">
      {%- for e in cv.expertise %}<li>{{ e }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <div class="toolkit__grid">
      {%- for t in cv.tools %}
      <div class="kit">
        <h3>{{ t.group }}</h3>
        <ul>{%- for i in t.items %}<li>{{ i }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="contact" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Contact</span>
    <h2 id="contact-heading">Need words that <em>work</em>? Let's talk.</h2>
    <a class="contact__mail" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>
    <p>I'm a content designer based in {{ site.location }}, open to roles in content design, UX writing and content strategy.</p>
  </div>
</section>
